To &lt;The Depot Management Staff&gt;

I'm heavily in favour to the one-hour mandatory lunch break, allowing us this break will give us time to refuel and relax. I'd like to make a claim that employees who do not have lunch, or a break, end up struggling with added stress. This time also allows us to decompress, and doesn't always have to involve food. According to recent surveys in Modern Workplace Trends, numerous employees have reported increased daily movement, and improved relationships. I'm on board with this survey, as this one-hour break is a lot more than just a lunch break. This hour will allow us to move around, go to the gym, socialize, and may even increase work productivity as it'll allow us to brainstorm during this time. Implementing this mandatory lunch break can also entice employees to be loyal to the company, as lunch breaks aren't a given everywhere else. Employees who are loyal to the company and work long overtime would also now have time to be able to connect with family. We can also use this mandatory lunch break to boast, as I'm sure employee satisfaction will be through the roof to try and garner new hires. A recent Career User Poll says that employees within the age groups of 18-24 (79% Voted Yes), and 25-39 (62% Voted Yes), state that "Break time is just as important as work time". People within the ages of 18-39 are at their prime time to look for a job, if our company states that we have mandatory lunch breaks, we'd be more likely to be chosen in favour over other companies. From the numerous health, social, and productivity benefits, implementing a mandatory lunch break has more pros than cons. I'm sure the majority of our employees would agree with me, and thank you for taking your time and reading this email.

- Depot Staff

Dear manager;

I am writing in concern of the mandatory one-hour lunch brake. I am concerned that people will take the one-hour brake and leave for there lunch break as they should, but they might not get back on time. They could be late for multiple reasons, like not paying attention to time, heavy traffic or construction. I personally don't think it should be mandatory for people to take a one-hour lunch brake. I think they should be able to work through lunch if they want to. Some people might need that one more hour of work to pay the bills. There also might be some people that stretch the one-hour lunch brake so they don't have to work as much.



Thanks for taking the time to hear my concerns regarding the one-hour lunch break. Sincerely Chase Ayers.

